   "color": "blue",
   "text": "The same menu everywhere a project shows up. On a chip it also has New thread; in the picker a tap already starts one, so only Edit and Delete."
  },
  {
   "id": "claude-2",
   "x": 1880,
   "y": 1100,
   "w": 320,
   "color": "blue",
   "text": "Icon kinds are the ones the server stores: an image from the folder (favicon), an emoji, or 1–2 letters on one of its colours. Drawing a new image stays with an agent on the Mac."
  },
  {
   "id": "claude-3",
   "x": 1410,
   "y": 2200,
   "w": 340,
   "color": "blue",
   "text": "I'd go with 5a: one system alert, the count is right on the red button. 5b says the same at more length. Threads are deleted for good, the folder on the Mac stays."
  },
